  "notes": "Breathy, low-dynamic electropop with a whisper-forward vocal. The drum claim is about what is missing: \"soft-transient programmed kick and clap, brushed 16th percussion, and a lot of negative space; tropical-house-derived pluck patterns stand in for hats on the dance records.\" So the snare transient is soft, `hihat.continuous` is false at `fillDensity` 0.1 with the roll vocabulary off, the perc bed is a brushed 16th shaker at a low gain, and the fills are pushed out to 16 bars — the negative space is the parameter. The low end is a synth sub with no 808 named, so no `bass808` block is authored; \"low end enters with the chorus and often carries the hook when the vocal stays static\" is a moderate `followRootsProb` with real passing motion rather than a root drone. Harmony is \"4-bar minor vamps\". The melody block is where the entry is most specific: \"a small-range mezzo instrument, deliberately written inside a 6th-to-9th span with breath and air as the expressive parameter rather than power\", so the register runs a 9th and no more, and \"the hook as a repeated two-note figure\" is `motifPitchCount` 2—3 — the smallest motif in this section. \"Toplines are conversational, written by the Michaels/Tranter axis for speech rhythm\" is the high step share and the syllabic density; \"harmony stacks are close and whispered\" is a low counter density. ⚠ `confidence` is medium and the research says why: \"writing axis, vocal character and palette documented; rhythmic/harmonic bands inferred\". Every drum probability, the humanize numbers, the harmonic families and `bpm.mode` 107 (the midpoint of the stated 90—125 band) are INFERRED. ⚠ The entry's [LOW-CONF] mark on the 6th-to-9th span claim is repeated here.",
